#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110293 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110672 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d203cc5-4e76-5f78-b431-b357164de3f9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Right Angles"}] :question/id #uuid "afde7d46-5a88-5ec8-b86f-32d126a36258" :question/math-academy-id "e-10595" :question/problem "Which of the following shows a right angle?\n\n![](images/e6/e6ee9f2a0b7dfa70c1d61dac0d19e1347d56ba94d93762c435d0727216d61143.png)" :question/worked-solution "An angle of $90^\\circ$ has the same measure as one-quarter of a full turn.\n\nAmong the given options, the only $90^\\circ$ angle is the following:\n\n![](images/b2/b2e63cd5919753a0b549f345ecfa5dbfa40bf5d85a3dbe8b59872119316d1dd7.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is II."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110294 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110673 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5701fed-0320-54da-8983-71c572ab1e8f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Straight Angles"}] :question/id #uuid "5427c83b-5f34-57fa-b56c-a0c190e74348" :question/math-academy-id "e-10596" :question/problem "Which of the following shows a straight angle?\n\n![](images/e6/e6ee9f2a0b7dfa70c1d61dac0d19e1347d56ba94d93762c435d0727216d61143.png)" :question/worked-solution "A straight angle has a degree measure of $180^\\circ$. This corresponds to one-half of a full turn.\n\nAmong the given options, the only straight angle is the following:\n\n![](images/1e/1e16add703d800bce68d70ded10f220808accb557ae15f9245147eaf3ca513b1.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is III."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110392 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b4df4d5-4ffc-53f0-8207-f710351f7456" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Null and Full Angles"}] :question/id #uuid "154c65b2-4d51-5da0-b00c-293f3fba3bd0" :question/math-academy-id "e-2604" :question/problem "![](images/86/867b3664e93f42c55a2f97dc28bf66794484e226981632c85f725926cec77def.png)\n\nWhat type of angle is $\\angle RST$, shown in the figure above?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the vertex of $\\angle RST$ is point $S$, not point $T$. So $\\angle RST$ is *not* a straight angle.\n\nAs a result, the two rays $\\overset{\\longrightarrow}{SR}$ and $\\overset{\\longrightarrow}{ST}$ of our angle coincide. So, we can think of $\\angle RST$ as:\n\n- A *null* angle, assuming it doesn't turn at all.\n\n![](images/a8/a8916a724d4463bf2047c919b73770160d3124838b61af0dcdc2b9e04322381a.png)\n\n- A *full* angle, assuming it makes one full turn.\n\n![](images/9c/9cd768b4361e95a18ffa52d6315fb5ea6cd0cf6784bc4c9e12b1bae1f6566755.png)\n\nSo, the answer is \"Null\" or \"Full.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110922 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110672 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d203cc5-4e76-5f78-b431-b357164de3f9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Right Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ceac1dc-f8ce-5325-a6d1-baa60da8fa4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2c/2c4f4a2ba45e3d499063f92dc615370542ce844b1b7b59eea18de7661568b568.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107424} {:answer/id #uuid "ee93e7dc-d4bf-5115-a2c0-fa59d5c72e86" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fc/fc6ab770cfd44992dfc1b2d927d1682f67817effbaaf481bba36fb648b5f24c7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107425} {:answer/id #uuid "f1db921a-bce3-51da-b5b9-215fa45a1ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ca/caeec49479f11a73e8afcddfa6e96749e1177f45fb45b5b210840ef99f744779.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107426} {:answer/id #uuid "51e32060-e079-5851-895d-8f63f09c71e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/32/32cb504e1be793e7f76c6f50c62598611fdb1a68f2276bb44273efdf8fd820fd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107427} {:answer/id #